  "details": "What methods does VRchat use to bake assets and Avatars that are used within it?\n\nWorlds and avatars should be baked when sent to players.\n\nYou can tell they are not, because massive memory leaks follow players between worlds. Avatars that are no longer in range of your player stay loaded in and do not leave until you restart the client.\n\nIts easy to tell. Just go to a populated world, the load will pick up on the computer's memory. Go to a completely empty world, with nothing but a floor... and the memory load will remain high.\n\nMost game providers who don't have reliable automated clearing methods, allow the user to choose an option to clear all cache memory while the game is running.\n\nYou could even put a limit on the amount of memory that can be used toward avatars, and allow the user to have preference flags, such as \"Friends First\", or the ability to temporarily mark individuals for loading, and everyone outside of this will be subject to the capacity's whims.",
